        "scope": "candidate_match_report",
        "excerpts": [
          "“I managed to serve well,” said Medvedev, who won 83 per cent (34/41) of first-serve points, according to Infosys ATP Stats. “It’s a very fast indoor court, so the serve is important. He managed to [serve] well in the break points in the first set. There was one point where I could have done a tiny bit better, but other than that he was serving well. I’m happy I managed to stay tough and get the win.”",
          "Medvedev continued to apply significant pressure throughout the second set and, unlike in the first, Cobolli was unable to withstand it, eventually succumbing to his opponent’s consistent baseline game to drop serve in the seventh game. The 2020 champion then continued to deliver a near-flawless serving performance to edge closer to victory before improving to 3-1 in their Lexus ATP Head2Head series."
        ],
